Z||000021||fieroshop||05-16-2000||11:43 AM||||Hey Haze_performance, DUH, I think you are a little too far from me to make it worthwhile, but I am sure you can build it yourself and save some money. If you need help feel free to call me and I will tell you how it was done. It really is not to hard to do.<BR>Since you are going to use a snow blower you can also build an induction system that will give you about 120 hp more. This way you can have a subwoofer system and a cowl induction system at the same time.<p>[This message has been edited by fieroshop (edited 05-16-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000022||tgowens||05-16-2000||01:06 PM||||Actually, all you guys are waaaaay off base, It is not only a sub-woofer and a cowl induction system but when I pull into a quarter car wash I don't even have to get out of the car to vacuum it out!! (gotta make sure the CD's don't get sucked up tho!!) - then again - maybe that big box on the back is really a 1,542 CD changer?<P>(By the way Cutter, there is a General Electric J-79 jet engine with afterburner under that Fiero plenum!)||||reg||1
